1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,545
The original nonlinear magnetostatic model used a two millimetre nonmagnetic target and gave ninety five point one millitesla mean parallel field near its surface

2
00:00:10,545 --> 00:00:12,759
That is an earlier target revision

3
00:00:12,759 --> 00:00:22,133
This updated assessment samples the saved fine mesh solution a quarter millimetre above the current three point one seven five millimetre target

4
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:27,080
The calculated mean parallel field is eighty six point four three millitesla

5
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:37,040
The range is eighty two point nine six to eighty nine point five three, with a mean normal field zero contour radius of twenty point one nine millimetres

6
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:45,178
The changed target, copper and fittings have unit relative permeability in this model, and the magnets and yoke are unchanged

7
00:00:45,178 --> 00:00:48,172
This supports resampling the existing solution

8
00:00:48,172 --> 00:00:55,789
It is not a new mesh or nonlinear solve, and it does not establish new uncertainty bounds or experimental validation.
